* Type parameters

⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000001⟫ functions can be written to work on multiple types using type parameters. The
type parameters of a function appear between brackets, before the function's
arguments.

⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000002⟫

This declaration means that ⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000003⟫s⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000004⟫ is a slice of any type ⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000005⟫T⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000006⟫ that fulfills the
built-in constraint ⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000007⟫comparable⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000008⟫. ⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000009⟫x⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000010⟫ is also a value of the same type.

⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000011⟫comparable⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000012⟫ is a useful constraint that makes it possible to use the ⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000013⟫==⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000014⟫ and
⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000015⟫!=⟪GTI18N_01a04510_000016⟫ operators on values of the type. In this example, we use it to compare a
